{
    "overview": "Enhance the LLM stream output display to show content previews with ellipsis for tool calls and auxiliary message types, similar to how text chunks are currently handled. This improves visibility into tool invocations and their results without overwhelming the console output with full content.",
    "architecture_decisions": [
        {
            "decision": "Use a centralized truncation utility function for consistent preview formatting",
            "rationale": "Centralizing the truncation logic ensures consistent behavior across all display locations (tool calls, tool results, text chunks) and makes it easier to adjust preview length globally",
            "alternatives_considered": "Inline truncation in each display location was rejected because it leads to inconsistent formatting and harder maintenance"
        },
        {
            "decision": "Extract and display key tool input parameters rather than the entire JSON input",
            "rationale": "Full JSON can be verbose; showing key parameters (like tool name and primary arguments) provides context without clutter. The exact parameters to show depend on the tool type",
            "alternatives_considered": "Showing full JSON input was rejected because it can be very long and overwhelm the console output"
        },
        {
            "decision": "Maintain backward compatibility with existing message formatters",
            "rationale": "The changes should not break existing functionality or alter the underlying data structures, only enhance the display layer",
            "alternatives_considered": "Modifying the message data structures was rejected to avoid breaking changes to the LLM calling protocol"
        }
    ],
    "components": [
        {
            "name": "Truncation Utility",
            "responsibilities": "Provide a consistent string truncation function with configurable max length and ellipsis indicator",
            "interfaces": "def truncate_preview(text: str, max_length: int = 60, ellipsis_str: str = '...') -> str"
        },
        {
            "name": "StreamJSONTracker (llm_caller.py)",
            "responsibilities": "Process streaming JSON lines from LLM, detect message types (text, tool_use, tool_result), and format display output with previews",
            "interfaces": "process_line(line: str) -> None - handles message type detection and delegates to formatters"
        },
        {
            "name": "Tool Call Formatter",
            "responsibilities": "Extract relevant tool input parameters and format them into a concise preview string",
            "interfaces": "format_tool_use_preview(tool_name: str, input_data: dict) -> str"
        },
        {
            "name": "Tool Result Formatter",
            "responsibilities": "Extract and format tool result content into a preview, handling different result types (text, JSON, error)",
            "interfaces": "format_tool_result_preview(result_data: Any) -> str"
        },
        {
            "name": "NDJSON Renderer (chat_history.py)",
            "responsibilities": "Render conversation history for human viewing with formatted tool call and result previews",
            "interfaces": "_render_ndjson_for_human(messages: List[dict]) -> str"
        }
    ],
    "data_flow": "1) LLM streams JSON chunks via SSE -> 2) StreamJSONTracker.process_line() receives each line -> 3) Message type detected (text/tool_use/tool_result) -> 4) Content extracted and passed to appropriate formatter -> 5) Formatter uses truncation utility to create preview -> 6) Formatted output displayed to console -> 7) For chat history rendering, _render_ndjson_for_human() iterates messages and applies same formatters -> 8) Consistent previews shown in history view",
    "implementation_plan": [
        "Create or identify the truncation utility function (truncate_preview) for consistent ellipsis handling",
        "Modify StreamJSONTracker.process_line() in llm_caller.py to extract tool input parameters and display with truncation when tool_use messages are received",
        "Enhance tool_use message handling to show formatted preview: 'Tool: <name> | Input: <param1>=<value1>, ...'",
        "Update tool_result message handling in process_line() to show content preview with truncation instead of just status",
        "Modify _render_ndjson_for_human() in chat_history.py to use the same formatting logic for tool calls and results",
        "Optionally update format_conversation_for_llm() to apply consistent truncation if it displays auxiliary messages",
        "Add tests for truncation utility with various edge cases (empty string, exact length, unicode)",
        "Add tests for tool preview formatters with different tool types and input structures",
        "Verify integration by running se3 run and observing tool call output in console"
    ],
    "testing_strategy": "Unit tests for truncation utility covering edge cases (empty strings, exact length matches, unicode characters, very long strings). Unit tests for tool formatters with various tool types (Read, Edit, Bash, etc.) and input structures. Integration tests verifying the full flow from LLM stream to console output. Manual verification by running se3 run on a task that triggers tool calls and confirming the output format matches the design with appropriate ellipsis."
}

